      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Arthroscopy Association of North America. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Non-arthroplasty treatment options for pseudoparalysis of the shoulder are preferable in the younger patient population. Although there are differing philosophies among shoulder surgeons, many prefer to avoid reversed total shoulder arthroplasty for patients under age 60 years. Arthroscopically assisted latissimus dorsi transfer may be a good alternative for these patients, but how the results compare with arthroscopic superior capsular reconstruction is the question."
      },
